  "narrative": "No assessments are due and independent validation capacity is exhausted, so I register discovery refinements that are directly tied to the only newly accepted interaction, H270, and to a small set of specificity tests for that interaction. First, P1 is the complement simple effect for H270: feature_063=1 versus 0 in the clean residual population lacking feature_037, feature_010, feature_002, feature_003, and feature_041, but in the feature_038<0 half. The accepted H270 interaction, signed to direction -1 with estimate +0.701 and lower bound +0.535, is evidence that the feature_063 contrast differs strongly between feature_038 halves. Because the clean residual full contrast has been negative raw, the plausible low-feature_038 simple contrast is positive raw or null. I therefore register direction +1 to test the scientifically meaningful possibility that feature_063=1 is associated with higher outcome_001 in low feature_038 contexts. A signed positive estimate and signed lower bound above 0.15 would support that reversal; a negative or imprecise result would favor null or weak residual effect. P2 and P3 test whether the accepted feature_038 modification is assay-specific or replicated by other standardized assays: in the same clean residual population, I ask whether the feature_063 lower-outcome association is stronger in the feature_018>=0 and feature_036>=0 halves. Direction -1 encodes the falsifiable claim that high standardized assay values amplify the feature_063 lower-outcome contrast. These interactions are expected to be uncertain; replication by feature_018 or feature_036 would make the feature_038 finding less likely to be an arbitrary single-assay fluctuation. P4-P6 test whether feature_038 also modifies the dominant marker associations in otherwise clean contexts. P4 asks whether feature_037=1 is associated with a stronger lower-outcome contrast when feature_038 is high, after excluding feature_010, feature_002, feature_003, feature_041, and feature_063. P5 and P6 ask whether feature_010=1 and feature_002=1 show stronger higher-outcome contrasts when feature_038 is high, after excluding the other dominant markers and residual feature_063. The directions encode plausible amplification: feature_037 lower-outcome effect stronger in high feature_038 for P4, and feature_010 or feature_002 higher-outcome effects stronger in high feature_038 for P5 and P6. Anticipated directions are uncertain because the dominant marker pattern is already robust and may not require feature_038 modification. If these dominant-marker interactions are null, it would strengthen the interpretation that feature_038 mainly modifies the context-restricted feature_063 residual association rather than acting as a general modifier. All proposals use mean_difference or interaction in the supplied dataset, return values already signed to the claimed direction, and remain subject to the 20-observation-per-cell rule; insufficient cells are feasibility failures, not evidence of absence. I continue to require that a new claim be accepted only when the signed point estimate and signed 95 percent Welch lower bound both exceed 0.15 composite dependency-score units in the claimed direction. All conclusions remain dataset-specific associations and do not imply causality, biological mechanism, gene or pathway assignment, or external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 20 exploration. Validation capacity exhausted; no further validation requests. Continue interpreting the accepted feature_063-by-feature_038 interaction in H270, not treating it as biological. The dominant supported dataset-specific associations remain: feature_037=1 lower outcome_001; feature_010=1 higher outcome_001; feature_002=1 higher outcome_001. feature_063 is a context-restricted lower-outcome residual marker in clean residual contexts, with accepted interaction H270 indicating stronger lower-outcome contrast in feature_038>=0. New priority: estimate the feature_038<0 simple effect, then decide whether low-feature_038 feature_063 is null, weakly negative, or reverses positive. Also test whether feature_018 and feature_036 replicate the feature_038 modification, and whether feature_038 also modifies feature_037, feature_010, or feature_002 in clean contexts. If the feature_038 modification is specific to feature_063 and the low simple effect is null/reverse, characterize feature_063 narrowly as a residual marker whose apparent effect depends strongly on standardized-assay strata and dominant-marker exclusions. If interactions with feature_018 or feature_036 are accepted, interpret the modification as broader within the constructed standardized-assay block but still not biological. If dominant-marker interactions are accepted, reconsider feature_038 as a more general modifier of dependency-score associations in this dataset. Avoid further broad post hoc Welch splits and avoid claims about broad feature_063, feature_003, feature_041, feature_038 main effects, or rare nominal contrasts. Ideal future method remains prespecified multivariable modeling or external validation with multiplicity control; none is currently available."
